# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Convex backend environment — informational only
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# You normally do NOT create a backend .env by hand.
#
# 1. Local deployment vars (CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT, CONVEX_URL, …) are
#    written automatically into .env.local the first time you run:
#
#        npx convex dev
#
#    Leave those to the CLI — don't set them here.
#
# 2. Server-side secrets are NOT stored in any file. They live in
#    the Convex deployment itself. Set each one with:
#
#        npx convex env set OPENAI_API_KEY <your-key>
#
#    (or via the Convex dashboard → Settings → Environment Variables).
#    List what's currently set with `npx convex env list`.
#
# Required server-side secrets:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY            Embeddings + LLM calls
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY         Claude calls (evaluator, agent, livechat)
#   CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN   Validates Clerk JWTs (convex/auth.config.ts)
#
# Optional server-side secrets:
#   COHERE_API_KEY            Only for the Cohere rerank step
#   LANGSMITH_API_KEY         Only for LangSmith dataset/experiment sync
